<title>USA: Case to repurchase up to 4 mln shares.</title>
<headline>Case to repurchase up to 4 mln shares.</headline>
<dateline>RACINE, Wis. 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Case Corp said Wednesday that its board of directors has authorized the purchase of up to four million shares of the company's common stock from time to time.  </p>
<p>The buyback represents about five percent of Case's 74 million common shares outstanding.</p>
<p>Timing of the buyback will be determined by financial and market conditions, the farming and construction equipment maker said.</p>
<p>Case shares were up 4-1/4 at 61-3/4 at mid-afternoon. The stock has benefited over the past two days from a strong industry forecast Tuesday by competitor Deere &amp; Co.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
